  "user_request_original": "Optimize an 8-layer dielectric anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate. Stack sequence: Air | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Silicon (semi-infinite). All 8 layer thicknesses are optimizable variables bounded 20-400 nm. Initialize thicknesses at: Ta2O5 layers [55, 165, 155, 45] nm and SiO2 layers [135, 245, 125, 35] nm (dual-band quarter-wave estimates at 1310 nm and 1550 nm centers). Use differential_evolution_thickness optimizer with population_size=50, max_iterations=500. Evaluate unpolarized reflectance and transmittance at 0 deg incidence across wavelength bands 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Objective: minimize weighted mean reflectance across both bands equally. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
